--TEST--
`clone` of a call to a generator does not compile — `rule:iteration/generator-stays-in-one-isolate`
--FILE--
<?nvs
// covers: lang:iteration/generators
// The call names a method whose body holds a `yield`, so the checker knows the
// operand is a generator and refuses the copy before the program runs.
class Count {
    public static function oneTwo(): Iterator<int> {
        yield 1;
        yield 2;
    }
}

var $copy = clone Count::oneTwo();
echo "unreachable\n";
--EXPECT--

--EXPECTF-ERROR--
error[E0858]: `clone` cannot copy a generator, and `Count::oneTwo` returns one
%A
error: aborting due to 1 error
To read what a code means and how to fix it, run `nvs agent show <code>`.
